ier), be righteous","n":36,"o":"MAT11:19 MAT12:37 LUK7:29 LUK7:35 LUK10:29 LUK16:15 LUK18:14 ACT13:39 ROM2:13 ROM3:4 ROM3:20 ROM3:24 ROM3:26 ROM3:28 ROM3:30 ROM4:2 ROM4:5 ROM5:1 ROM5:9 ROM6:7 ROM8:30 ROM8:33 1CO4:4 1CO6:11 GAL2:16 GAL2:17 GAL3:8 GAL3:11 GAL3:24 GAL5:4 1TI3:16 TIT3:7 JAS2:21 JAS2:24 JAS2:25 REV22:11"},"G1355":{"lemma":"διόπερ","translit":"dióper","derivation":"from G1352 (διό) and G4007 (περ);","strongs_def":" on which very account","kjv_def":"wherefore","n":3,"o":"1CO8:13 1CO10:14 1CO14:13"},"G1369":{"lemma":"διχάζω","translit":"dicházō","derivation":"from a derivative of G1364 (δίς);","strongs_def":" to make apart, i.e. sunder (figuratively, alienate)","kjv_def":"set at variance","n":1,"o":"MAT10:35"},"G1341":{"lemma":"δικαιοκρισία","translit":"dikaiokrisía","derivation":"from G1342 (δίκαιος) and G2920 (κρίσις);","strongs_def":" a just sentence","kjv_def":"righteous judgment","n":1,"o":"ROM2:5"},"G1345":{"lemma":"δικαίωμα","translit":"dikaíōma","derivation":"from G1344 (δικαιόω);","strongs_def":" an equitable deed; by implication, a statute or decision","kjv_def":"judgment, justification, ordinance, righteousness","n":10,"o":"LUK1:6 ROM1:32 ROM2:26 ROM5:16 ROM5:18 ROM8:4 HEB9:1 HEB9:10 REV15:4 REV19:8"},"G1301":{"lemma":"διατηρέω","translit":"diatēréō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G5083 (τηρέω);","strongs_def":" to watch thoroughly, i.e. (positively and transitively) to observe strictly, or (negatively and reflexively) to avoid wholly","kjv_def":"keep","n":2,"o":"LUK2:51 ACT15:29"},"G1390":{"lemma":"δόμα","translit":"dóma","derivation":"from the base of G1325 (δίδωμι);","strongs_def":" a present","kjv_def":"gift","n":4,"o":"MAT7:11 LUK11:13 EPH4:8 PHP4:17"},"G1356":{"lemma":"διοπετής","translit":"diopetḗs","derivation":"from the alternate of G2203 (Ζεύς) and the alternate of G4098 (πίπτω);","strongs_def":" sky-fallen (i.e. an aerolite)","kjv_def":"which fell down from Jupiter","n":1,"o":"ACT19:35"},"G1319":{"lemma":"διδασκαλία","translit":"di