:"MAT14:31 MAT28:17"},"G1348":{"lemma":"δικαστής","translit":"dikastḗs","derivation":"from a derivative of G1349 (δίκη);","strongs_def":" a judger","kjv_def":"judge","n":3,"o":"LUK12:14 ACT7:27 ACT7:35"},"G1306":{"lemma":"διαυγάζω","translit":"diaugázō","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G826 (αὐγάζω);","strongs_def":" to glimmer through, i.e. break (as day)","kjv_def":"dawn","n":1,"o":"2PE1:19"},"G1392":{"lemma":"δοξάζω","translit":"doxázō","derivation":"from G1391 (δόξα);","strongs_def":" to render (or esteem) glorious (in a wide application)","kjv_def":"(make) glorify(-ious), full of (have) glory, honour, magnify","n":54,"o":"MAT5:16 MAT6:2 MAT9:8 MAT15:31 MRK2:12 LUK2:20 LUK4:15 LUK5:25 LUK5:26 LUK7:16 LUK13:13 LUK17:15 LUK18:43 LUK23:47 JHN7:39 JHN8:54 JHN11:4 JHN12:16 JHN12:23 JHN12:28 JHN13:31 JHN13:32 JHN14:13 JHN15:8 JHN16:14 JHN17:1 JHN17:4 JHN17:5 JHN17:10 JHN21:19 ACT3:13 ACT4:21 ACT11:18 ACT13:48 ACT21:20 ROM1:21 ROM8:30 ROM11:13 ROM15:6 ROM15:9 1CO6:20 1CO12:26 2CO3:10 2CO9:13 GAL1:24 2TH3:1 HEB5:5 1PE1:8 1PE2:12 1PE4:11 1PE4:14 1PE4:16 REV15:4 REV18:7"},"G1327":{"lemma":"διέξοδος","translit":"diéxodos","derivation":"from G1223 (διά) and G1841 (ἔξοδος);","strongs_def":" an outlet through, i.e. probably an open square (from which roads diverge)","kjv_def":"highway","n":0,"o":""},"G1311":{"lemma":"διαφθείρω","translit":"diaphtheírō","derivation":"from G1225 (διαβάλλω) and G5351 (φθείρω);","strongs_def":" to rot thoroughly, i.e. (by implication) to ruin (passively, decay utterly, figuratively, pervert)","kjv_def":"corrupt, destroy, perish","n":5,"o":"LUK12:33 2CO4:16 1TI6:5 REV8:9 REV11:18"},"G1384":{"lemma":"δόκιμος","translit":"dókimos","derivation":"from G1380 (δοκέω);","strongs_def":" properly, acceptable (current after assayal), i.e. approved","kjv_def":"approved, tried","n":7,"o":"ROM14:18 ROM16:10 1CO11:19 2CO10:18 2CO13:7 2TI2:15 JAS1:12"},"G1362":{"lemma":"διπλοῦς","translit":"diploûs","derivation":"from G1364 (δίς) and (probably) the base of G41